WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:02.830
It’s a tough job market out there right
now.

00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:07.350
It feels like everyone is either being laid
off, furloughed, stuck in a dead-end position

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:12.230
at a job with no prospects of career advancement,
or working multiple jobs just to meet the

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:16.240
bills every month, as you’re slowly driven
into the ground.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:19.019
If only somewhere new was hiring.

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:20.990
Somewhere exciting.

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:25.999
Somewhere where every day is an adventure
and you never truly know what you can expect.

00:00:25.999 --> 00:00:28.970
Well, lucky for you, there is such a place.

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:35.390
It’s the SCP Foundation, and after a recent
high-casualty SCP-682 breach, they have plenty

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:38.610
of new positions open for go-getters just
like you!

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:43.911
That’s why we put out a post on our community
page asking for the job at the SCP Foundation

00:00:43.911 --> 00:00:47.640
you think you’d be best at, and your reasons
for why.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:51.570
And today, we’re going to evaluate your
answers, and see who’s up to the task!

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:52.850
Let’s go.

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:56.970
Javier Gomez de Lara Santos said, “I don't
know if it counts, but being on the part of

00:00:56.970 --> 00:01:02.970
relocating safe SCP that are "rehabilitated"
such as SCP-2273 would be a very wholesome

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:07.480
experience to see them enjoying human company
once more ( other than doctors and security

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:12.250
officers ) and you could get some new extraordinary
friendships such as Alexei Belitrov had with

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:13.490
his psychiatrist.”

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:16.880
We thought we’d start this video off on
a nice wholesome one.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:21.109
In any kind of Broken Veil scenario, it’s
natural that some of the nicer anomalies,

00:01:21.109 --> 00:01:25.960
like Belitrov, the Reluctant Dimension Hopper,
and the Abdominal Planet guy would be released

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:27.630
back into civilian life.

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:32.030
Of course, to get a job helping this happen,
much like Alexei Belitrov’s psychiatrist,

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:37.069
you’d likely need to be qualified in social
work, psychology, or psychiatry.

00:01:37.069 --> 00:01:40.490
But it’s probably one of the more fulfilling
jobs you can get with the Foundation.

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:46.979
Geologyhill123 said, “Having an MA in history,
I can see myself working as a researcher into

00:01:46.979 --> 00:01:50.250
ancient anomalies and finding their cultural
origins.

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:54.549
Plotting the Aristocrats family tree - although
knowing the Habsburg lineage it's more of

00:01:54.549 --> 00:01:56.310
a shrub - would be fascinating!

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:59.420
The wanderer’s library sounds like a dream
come true as well.”

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:02.209
Ah, now this is a fun one.

00:02:02.209 --> 00:02:07.700
Seeing as anomalies can manifest in everything
from ancient ruins like SCP-2621 to extinct

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:12.760
cultures like the Daevites to twisted family
lines like The Aristocrats, taking a historical

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:17.830
approach to exploring SCPs is definitely a
valuable job, and one perfectly suited to

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:20.200
people with a background in history.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:23.129
Just be careful with some of those ancient
texts.

00:02:23.129 --> 00:02:28.180
Reading the wrong ones might lead to certain
strange mental and physical changes…

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:35.010
Suicunefan123 said, “I’d love to work
in virology within the foundation, specifically

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:38.030
writing the reports for the more math-minded
folks in the field.

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:40.420
In my experience, they need the help!

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:44.680
Ensuring reports are clear, concise, and useful
would be my ideal placement.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:47.030
Dream job in reality, too…”

00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:51.330
Virology is an undeniably useful skill for
work at the SCP Foundation, given the number

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:57.519
of terrifying viruses they deal with, like
the incurable contagious zombie virus, SCP-008,

00:02:57.519 --> 00:03:02.569
the Sarkic nightmare that is SCP-610, the
Flesh that Hates, or the considerably more

00:03:02.569 --> 00:03:07.930
technological infection, SCP-217, the Clockwork
Virus.

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:10.959
And hey, somebody needs to write those reports!

00:03:10.959 --> 00:03:15.099
Drew Sklar said, “As an engineer, I feel
like doing researching and development for

00:03:15.099 --> 00:03:17.700
containment procedures would be so interesting.

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:22.760
The conditions a cell has to meet vary so
much between SCPs, and each one is so strange

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:25.090
and interesting that it feels like a puzzle.”

00:03:25.090 --> 00:03:30.270
Containment specialists are a vital part of
the operations of the SCP Foundation, considering

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:32.500
that containment is one of their core principles.

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:37.450
It’s an exciting and intellectually stimulating
job, but there’s also a lot of pressure

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:38.450
involved.

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:41.600
Knowing, if you don’t do your job right,
you could be responsible for a breach that

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:46.350
leads to a huge number of deaths for your
fellow personnel, the civilian world, and

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:48.010
potentially even you.

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:49.920
We’re sure you’ll do fine, though.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:51.310
No need to stress…

00:03:51.310 --> 00:03:54.010
Celi Phon said, “Personally, I'd want to
work in amnestics.

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:58.269
You don't have to interact with dangerous
anomalies, just your fellow foundation coworkers.

00:03:58.269 --> 00:04:03.090
I doubt the job is anywhere near as insane
as research staff or mtf.

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:06.140
Being a foundation middle(wo)man suits me
just fine.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:10.450
In with the Class A/B amnestic and out with
the cognitohazard my friends!”

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:12.020
That’s a great attitude!

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:16.329
And honestly, there are a lot of benefits
to working directly with amnestics.

00:04:16.329 --> 00:04:20.620
Fun fact: Every time we have a video that
underperforms, we release an amnestic gas

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:23.009
onto our audience, and release it again later.

00:04:23.009 --> 00:04:26.440
Who knows how many times you’ve listened
to the sentence you’re listening to right

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:27.440
now?

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:28.440
Moving on.

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:33.060
Tim West said, “I would go with where my
experience helps me excel at the most.

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:37.400
I've been working as a PSO (protective service
officer) for the Department of Homeland security

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:40.520
for some years now, I also worked as an armed
bouncer.

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:44.780
Was trained in the use of force, defensive
tactics, training with firearms, long guns,

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:46.590
and unarmed combat.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:50.060
Also trained for bomb detection and use of
magnetometer's.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:53.280
For the SCP Foundation, I would apply for
the security division.”

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:56.960
Well, Tim, you seem pretty much perfectly
qualified for the job.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:58.280
When can you start?

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:00.050
No, seriously, can you start right now?

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:04.290
SCP-106 just got out again and we really need
a hand getting him back under control.

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:06.229
It’s an all-hands-on-deck situation.

00:05:06.229 --> 00:05:08.949
Oh no, he’s coming through the wall, oh
god--

00:05:08.949 --> 00:05:13.561
Grand-Admiral Batch said, “I’d go for
Containment Specialist, Occult Section, as

00:05:13.561 --> 00:05:15.700
I am very well versed in the occult.

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:19.530
As to where I’d exceed others, probably
when it comes to rituals, as I have an interest

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:23.919
in them and know a lot about them, including
some, let’s say, practical experience.”

00:05:23.919 --> 00:05:25.430
Huh…

00:05:25.430 --> 00:05:28.370
Are we allowed to ask follow-up questions?

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:32.550
Because I’m now really, really curious about
your occult experience, Grand-Admiral Batch.

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:34.930
We’ll dispatch a field agent shortly.

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:39.479
Meta Man said, “I don’t really know much
about the rankings or positions in the foundation,

00:05:39.479 --> 00:05:44.139
but if there was a job for deciding who/what
gets sent where for testing, I would do that.

00:05:44.139 --> 00:05:47.660
I could do cross-testing as well as just having
the ability to have my worst enemies killed

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:49.370
by an SCP.”

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:53.979
See, applications like this are why we do
background checks, Meta Man.

00:05:53.979 --> 00:05:58.379
You need to ascend to the level of O5 Council
before you can start using anomalies to belligerently

00:05:58.379 --> 00:06:01.260
assassinate your enemies without consequences.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:04.919
Doing it on any level below that is more than
likely to get you into some serious trouble

00:06:04.919 --> 00:06:06.500
with your Site Director.

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:07.500
MissingNo.

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:11.259
Said, “I’m proficient with firearms, and
have been refurbishing weapons and doing some

00:06:11.259 --> 00:06:16.030
pretty decent gunsmithing for parts that I
need/need fixed up for the past 10 years.

00:06:16.030 --> 00:06:20.129
I’d have an undying loyalty to the foundation,
and maybe have a chance to work with some

00:06:20.129 --> 00:06:23.750
of that fancy anomalous weaponry, or just
a hired MTF guard.

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:25.229
(The first would be fun.)

00:06:25.229 --> 00:06:29.020
Or I could just be Dr. Bright’s newest body,
or fodder for 682.

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:30.020
Whatever works.”

00:06:30.020 --> 00:06:33.350
Well, we appreciate the fact that you’re
giving yourself a wide range of options here

00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:38.600
- Especially considering that being a vessel
for Dr. Bright or fodder for SCP-682 has a

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:40.910
very low barrier to entry.

00:06:40.910 --> 00:06:44.560
But hey, considering that MTF operatives are
often killed in the line of duty, it’s likely

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:47.710
that a position will be open for you if you
can prove yourself.

00:06:47.710 --> 00:06:52.449
EllisBellis13 said, “I think I would be
a researcher trying to understand anomalies

00:06:52.449 --> 00:06:55.240
who seemingly break the laws of physics and
the universe.

00:06:55.240 --> 00:07:00.330
I am studying math and physics and currently
doing my bachelor’s thesis on quantum bits.

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:04.720
By understanding the physics allowing the
anomalies to behave anomalously, we could

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:07.800
utilize the knowledge to develop new cool
technologies.”

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:09.810
We like your style, Ellis.

00:07:09.810 --> 00:07:11.800
We need people like you on the team.

00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:15.409
Just make sure that while developing this
new physics-bending technology, you don’t

00:07:15.409 --> 00:07:17.659
wind up trapping yourself in the Red Reality.

00:07:17.659 --> 00:07:21.039
But hey, at least you’d be able to keep
Dr. Scranton company.

00:07:21.039 --> 00:07:25.030
Eric Back said, “I'd love to work with the
technical side of the whole foundation, could

00:07:25.030 --> 00:07:28.889
be anything from IT to constructing the containments
used on SCP's.”

00:07:28.889 --> 00:07:29.889
Yes!

00:07:29.889 --> 00:07:30.889
Please!

00:07:30.889 --> 00:07:33.229
You could act as a replacement for Technical
Director Rosen.

00:07:33.229 --> 00:07:35.069
Seriously, he’s utterly unbearable.

00:07:35.069 --> 00:07:36.570
We need to get rid of that jerk.

00:07:36.570 --> 00:07:38.410
Krizia said, “Would probably be in MTF Mu-13
(Ghostbusters).

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:44.750
I have always been fascinated with the supernatural-
that, and my sensitivity to the paranormal

00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:48.979
and seemingly paranormal would definitely
make me a valuable asset to the team.”

00:07:48.979 --> 00:07:51.010
You seem like a great fit for the team.

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:53.879
We just hope that Ghost-busting makes you
feel good.

00:07:53.879 --> 00:07:58.229
PsychoCobra Gaming said, “Having a background
in Psychiatry, I immediately go to the idea

00:07:58.229 --> 00:08:02.419
that all of the stress and threat of constant
death would really weigh on the mind of the

00:08:02.419 --> 00:08:03.419
employees.

00:08:03.419 --> 00:08:07.349
I’m not sure if The Foundation has a psychiatric
department but if I could spearhead the creation

00:08:07.349 --> 00:08:11.070
of one, then that would also give room to
climb up the hierarchy of The Foundation.

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:15.450
I’m sure Dr. Bright must have PTSD from
his several deaths and the 05 Council must

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:18.669
have some form of mental anguish from their
centuries of life.”

00:08:18.669 --> 00:08:23.289
Oh yeah, we imagine it’d indicate that something
is very wrong if a seasoned Foundation employee

00:08:23.289 --> 00:08:25.939
doesn’t have a little PTSD on the books.

00:08:25.939 --> 00:08:30.500
The scary thing is, with some of the poor
folks at the SCP Foundation, them recounting

00:08:30.500 --> 00:08:34.130
their days might give their therapists PTSD.

00:08:34.130 --> 00:08:38.330
Stonewood Studios said, “Some kind of mechanical
engineering profession.

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:40.909
Just being able to observe anomalous tech
would be incredible.

00:08:40.909 --> 00:08:45.510
I'd love to try to discern how 914 works,
or spend my days trying to understand the

00:08:45.510 --> 00:08:48.850
functionality of the numerous remnants of
the Broken God.”

00:08:48.850 --> 00:08:52.060
This seems like a good application of your
interests and skills.

00:08:52.060 --> 00:08:57.070
And if you want to be even better at engineering,
why not put yourself into the SCP-914 chamber

00:08:57.070 --> 00:08:59.050
and set it to Very Fine.

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:00.770
Just to see what happens, you know?

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:02.170
It’s a fun time.

00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:06.600
Frank Official said, “Honestly even just
being a janitor would satisfy me, there’s

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:10.389
this sense of dread knowing some sort of dangerous
thing could break out at any moment.

00:09:10.389 --> 00:09:11.600
Really does get your blood pumping.”

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:14.350
It’s a bold choice, honestly.

00:09:14.350 --> 00:09:18.660
All the danger and stress of working for the
SCP Foundation, without any of the clearance,

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:19.780
pay, or prestige.

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:22.100
You’re playing 5D Chess.

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:26.111
Minty said, “I'd like to be part of some
kind of Foundation reintegration program where

00:09:26.111 --> 00:09:30.691
the SCPs are taught to control their powers
and just get used to being less deadly, so

00:09:30.691 --> 00:09:32.500
they could re-enter human society.

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:36.450
I just feel bad for the SCPs, being essentially
put in cages.

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:37.450
Some of them need a hug.

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:39.950
Barring that, I'd just sign up for the Serpent's
Hand.”

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:43.110
Considering the SCP Foundation can be a little…

00:09:43.110 --> 00:09:47.660
Cold, towards the anomalies, you may eventually
find yourself becoming disheartened towards

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:49.970
the Foundation and its practices.

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:54.750
At this point, yes, it seems likely that allegiance
with the Serpent’s Hand would be a pretty

00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:56.490
appealing prospect for you.

00:09:56.490 --> 00:10:01.000
Cat and Otter said, “I would enjoy some
good old low-risk humanoids.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:05.350
Have a nice chat with them, maybe go a round
of tennis with Cain, Iris, and Mr. Fish.”

00:10:05.350 --> 00:10:08.529
It would indeed be nice to chat with some
low-risk humanoids.

00:10:08.529 --> 00:10:13.529
Be warned about Mr. Fish, though, he’s been
known to be a little salty on occasion.

00:10:13.529 --> 00:10:19.060
Pikeshades said, “I suppose I would like
to work as an archivist in a records room

00:10:19.060 --> 00:10:21.640
cataloging anomalies and updating files.

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:26.910
I do that mostly in my IRL job, while also
turning old word document manuals into educational

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:27.910
videos.

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:31.639
So I could probably also collaborate with
doctors and researchers in how to make training

00:10:31.639 --> 00:10:37.279
videos for new D-Classes and MFTs in how to
deal and approach certain SCPs and/or rival

00:10:37.279 --> 00:10:38.450
organizations.”

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:40.010
Wait…

00:10:40.010 --> 00:10:44.160
You want to make training and informational
videos about SCPs?

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:47.329
That sounds to us like you want to be our
competition.

00:10:47.329 --> 00:10:53.440
Listen, buddy, we rule the fun, user-friendly
infographic videos about SCPs game.

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:55.509
You don’t want to step on our turf.

00:10:55.509 --> 00:10:57.339
We can be very aggressive.

00:10:57.339 --> 00:11:02.519
Gabbie said, “I think I would work in the
application and development of containment

00:11:02.519 --> 00:11:04.910
which would be less stressful for the SCP.

00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:08.459
My hope would be to make more of the sapient
SCPs comfortable.

00:11:08.459 --> 00:11:09.760
Hopefully befriend a few.

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:12.220
I would more than likely die within the first
week.

00:11:12.220 --> 00:11:15.540
But I hope at least I'd make someone or something
smile.”

00:11:15.540 --> 00:11:19.620
The SCP Foundation honestly needs more people
with a humanist approach like you.

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:23.870
There are plenty of perfectly friendly sapient
anomalies who deserve to have a nice, comfortable

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:26.640
pad while they’re contained by the SCP Foundation.

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:31.610
Do we really want God complaining about scoliosis
because his unpleasant Foundation cot doesn’t

00:11:31.610 --> 00:11:32.840
have enough padding?

00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:36.910
Just make sure you exercise caution when selecting
the anomalies you decide to give the fancy

00:11:36.910 --> 00:11:41.079
new digs to, seeing as some might use it as
a method of escape.

00:11:41.079 --> 00:11:47.090
That being said, if we gave SCP-106 or SCP-049
a high-quality jacuzzi in each of their cells,

00:11:47.090 --> 00:11:49.220
do you think they might chill out a little?

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:53.199
After all, we’ve never really tried “Making
the containment chamber too relaxing and chill

00:11:53.199 --> 00:11:54.970
to even want to leave.”

00:11:54.970 --> 00:11:58.480
Symphony In Blue said, “I think it would
be cool if there was a position where you

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:03.089
just visited/chilled with some of the friendly
scps, especially those who struggle with living

00:12:03.089 --> 00:12:04.200
in containment.

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:08.199
I feel like it would be really helpful for
them and their general wellbeing/mental health

00:12:08.199 --> 00:12:12.160
if they had someone who wasn’t explicitly
a researcher or doctor, but was rather just

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:16.889
somebody to talk to, to chill out with, and
to give them a little bit more normality.

00:12:16.889 --> 00:12:20.250
Might help people be a little more comfortable
and happy in containment.”

00:12:20.250 --> 00:12:23.110
Again, this is another pleasingly wholesome
one.

00:12:23.110 --> 00:12:25.630
A lot of these anomalies could use a friend
to chat with.

00:12:25.630 --> 00:12:28.690
Dr. Gears isn’t the most scintillating conversationalist.

00:12:28.690 --> 00:12:34.760
Lolchief119 said, “I'd probably enlist in
MTF Beta-7 the "Maz Hatters" because there

00:12:34.760 --> 00:12:38.950
was always this deep fascination about biohazard,
chemical, and radiological stuff that I’ve

00:12:38.950 --> 00:12:42.910
had for many years now, plus there is a great
chance I get to kill zombies!

00:12:42.910 --> 00:12:46.990
Maybe if I ask the Task force leader really
nicely, maybe I can carry a barbed wire bat

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:48.920
when clubbing said zombies!”

00:12:48.920 --> 00:12:53.770
Well, deciding to club anomalous zombies to
death with a Negan-style barbed wire bat would

00:12:53.770 --> 00:12:58.070
definitely earn you some points with other
weird, violent mavericks like Dr. Clef.

00:12:58.070 --> 00:13:03.029
In all likelihood, though, you’d be spending
most of the time in a heavy-duty hazmat suit,

00:13:03.029 --> 00:13:07.350
picking up dangerous waste material in the
aftermath of an anomalous attack.

00:13:07.350 --> 00:13:08.350
Have fun!

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:13.151
ChocolateQuill said, “I'm going to be completely
real with y'all: I like to THINK I'd be a

00:13:13.151 --> 00:13:15.329
high-level researcher for the foundation.

00:13:15.329 --> 00:13:19.339
But I'd probably get demoted for wanting to
play with SCP-999 all the time.”

00:13:19.339 --> 00:13:21.200
We appreciate your honesty.

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:24.649
And there are definitely worse things you
can get in trouble for doing at a Foundation

00:13:24.649 --> 00:13:28.190
containment site, like that one Brony researcher
who…

00:13:28.190 --> 00:13:30.890
Well, you know the story on that one.

00:13:30.890 --> 00:13:36.100
Brodie Insch said, “Well, I'm not going
to lie, I feel that I and SCP-049 have a lot

00:13:36.100 --> 00:13:40.940
in common (not the fact that we are both doctors
or kind of evil) but that we share a personality

00:13:40.940 --> 00:13:42.029
and a lot of mannerisms.

00:13:42.029 --> 00:13:46.389
If there was a job to study and interact with
a single subject that's right for me.

00:13:46.389 --> 00:13:51.610
(I also think it would be pleasurable to learn
from SCP-049 as we share a lot of mannerisms

00:13:51.610 --> 00:13:55.139
there is a chance I could possibly become
a "friend" of sorts and he could tell me all

00:13:55.139 --> 00:13:58.149
about how his bag works along with the language
he writes in).”

00:13:58.149 --> 00:14:00.080
Hey, this sounds excellent!

00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:04.959
We think SCP-049 would be elated to have a
new friend to discuss his thoughts and theories

00:14:04.959 --> 00:14:05.959
with.

00:14:05.959 --> 00:14:09.350
And having someone he sees as a peer would
be a great way to keep him mellow and stop

00:14:09.350 --> 00:14:11.149
him from breaching containment all the time.

00:14:11.149 --> 00:14:13.970
Maybe we’ve found the solution to one of
our oldest--

00:14:13.970 --> 00:14:14.970
Oh.

00:14:14.970 --> 00:14:15.970
Okay.

00:14:15.970 --> 00:14:18.680
Back to the drawing board, I guess.

00:14:18.680 --> 00:14:22.550
Imainaba said, “Personally, I would like
to be a part of the ethics committee.

00:14:22.550 --> 00:14:26.990
They're probably the most powerful group in
the SCP foundation besides the O5 council.

00:14:26.990 --> 00:14:29.670
I'd be able to access knowledge that most
staff can't.

00:14:29.670 --> 00:14:33.519
The most important part for me is that I'll
be able to make the experiments on the SCP's

00:14:33.519 --> 00:14:35.709
and the D-class less violent.

00:14:35.709 --> 00:14:37.370
They deserve some rights as well.”

00:14:37.370 --> 00:14:41.440
Wow, we really are learning that a lot of
our fans are surprisingly ethical people today.

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:44.670
It truly warms our SCP-058s.

00:14:44.670 --> 00:14:48.480
And it’s true, the Foundation really does
need the Ethics Committee to make sure that

00:14:48.480 --> 00:14:52.089
these monster hunters never become monsters
themselves.

00:14:52.089 --> 00:14:56.660
Angel Jaf Benitez said, “I'd love to work
with anomalous plants, either in the bioresearch

00:14:56.660 --> 00:15:00.850
zone or as a member of the gardeners, I just
like plants that much, even though I know

00:15:00.850 --> 00:15:02.980
what some plants are capable of.”

00:15:02.980 --> 00:15:07.820
Hey, the Foundation needs plenty of botanists
for their wide variety of plant-based anomalies.

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:11.639
And if you like your plants to have a little
bit of flesh on the side, you can head down

00:15:11.639 --> 00:15:16.480
to SCP-3989, the Bone Orchard, for the best
of both worlds!

00:15:16.480 --> 00:15:20.730
Thorn Wolfy said, “I'm an animal caretaker
with a Bachelor's in zoology, so I'd likely

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:22.699
be some kind of cryptid keeper.

00:15:22.699 --> 00:15:26.910
I'd do my best to ensure the more beast-like
SCPs were as comfortable as possible in their

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:31.890
enclosure while maintaining security and their
safety as well as the rest of the staff.

00:15:31.890 --> 00:15:36.270
I'd likely also advocate a bit for them, try
to keep too many inhumane experiments from

00:15:36.270 --> 00:15:37.270
happening.

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:38.790
No cruelty for cruelty's sake.”

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:44.329
Cryptid Keeper is a hell of a job title, as
long as you remember to stay safe out there.

00:15:44.329 --> 00:15:48.250
After all, some anomalies are more dangerous
than others, and it’s often rarely the ones

00:15:48.250 --> 00:15:49.250
you think.

00:15:49.250 --> 00:15:52.279
But we definitely respect your commitment
to keeping things humane.

00:15:52.279 --> 00:15:54.590
It’s always the best way to go.

00:15:54.590 --> 00:15:59.400
Wow, what an incredible interview session
- it’s looking like the SCP Foundation is

00:15:59.400 --> 00:16:03.829
going to have an awesome new stock of employees
on their hands once all the paperwork is through.

00:16:03.829 --> 00:16:08.019
And thanks to this organization’s incredibly
high turnaround, we’re sure that once all

00:16:08.019 --> 00:16:12.009
of these newbies are either nicely grizzled
or killed by an anomaly, we’ll get some

00:16:12.009 --> 00:16:14.329
new fresh faces around here real soon.

00:16:14.329 --> 00:16:18.040
Be sure to keep an eye on our community page
for the next chance to be a part of one of

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:20.399
these delightfully whacky videos!

00:16:20.399 --> 00:16:24.860
Now go check out “How to Work at the SCP
Foundation Explained” and “Good vs Evil

00:16:24.860 --> 00:16:30.019
- SCP Ethics Committee Orientation” for
more information on jobs and the inner workings

00:16:30.019 --> 00:16:30.820
of the SCP Foundation!

